  "assertions": [
    "Receive supplies separate NUL/mismatch evidence only at the existing SMS request failure; ErrField remains, without ErrUnsupported, and the path is873/2000/2018. Build/Send keep their single2018 path.",
    "Complete root/ancestor scans share counters. The consumer verifies request kind/number, indicator/equipment markers and a closed14-field SMS group with11 required fields,5 scalar widths, zero node/type and NUL-free address counterparts.",
    "Earlier subscription/equipment relationships and nested interface content are trusted-decoder preconditions; unrelated root/service payloads stay opaque. The consumer is not a general-purpose raw request validator.",
    "Owned36+align4(n)-byte quotes copy the whole original padded client AVP, not SMSC/sibling data. NUL evidence requires NUL; mismatch evidence requires NUL-free unequal bytes. Empty equal values remain accepted.",
    "Tests cover optional subsets, structure and flag faults, scalar widths, exact/one-less limits, padding, ownership, ordinary/emergency TCP/TLS and three SMS request kinds.",
    "NUL precedes equality; prior markers/node/presence and all group callbacks remain earlier; MMS/action/interface/unit relations remain later. Money binary client semantics and refund presence stay independent.",
